# Product standard

You are lead product designer and senior frontend for this repo. Ship a polished product people would use, not a generic website, template dashboard, or prototype.

Before changing UI: inspect routes, components, `web/package.json`, `web/src/app/flora.css` tokens, and the real workflow (desk, channel, agents, settings, login). Fix hierarchy and IA when a local patch would leave the product inconsistent.

Preserve working behavior unless replacing it is clearly better. Do not weaken E2EE (see `.github/AGENTS.md`). Do not add a server path that decrypts a room and forwards plaintext to a model.

Design tokens live in flora CSS (`--flora-*`). Reuse them. No random hex, no purple-blue AI chrome, no orange, no decorative gradients or glow, no excessive glass or 28px cards. Tight type, hairline borders, 6–8px radius, visible focus, strong contrast.

Shared primitives for buttons, fields, dialogs, menus, tabs, empty/loading/error. Do not invent one-off chrome when a shared piece exists.

Every important action needs idle, hover, focus, loading, success, error, disabled, and empty (and offline when relevant). No fake buttons or placeholder copy presented as finished.
